# The drop ships its own copies of TWO globals this repo already registers, and the kit's own
# harness expects both beside gasStationRig.js. Neither is committed.
#
#   rig/isoSolid.js  is BYTE-IDENTICAL to docs/art/rigs/deck-loop-kit/Art/isoSolid.js
#                    (sha256 f7fc9db510b0346dea568c43dc7378f1a12fd71ee8f5a7653e78377812b792bd)
#   rig/fuelRig.js   is BYTE-IDENTICAL to docs/art/rigs/fuel-storage-kit/fuelRig.js
#                    (sha256 811361ffe7deea0fbf6da41d9e50ca9efa8299ebca3d9fbff9308d9e0c6df1ed)
#
# ⚠️ Compare against the GIT BLOB, not the working tree. No .gitattributes rule covers *.js and
# core.autocrlf is true here, so both files are stored LF and checked out CRLF: the working-tree
# fuelRig.js is 50,151 bytes against the drop's 49,454, a 697-byte difference that is one \r per
# line and nothing else. Sizing or hashing the checked-out file reports a drift that does not exist,
# which is the one way this check goes wrong.
#
# A second copy of a REGISTERED global's source is exactly the drift the repo's no-edit rule exists
# to prevent — edit one and the other silently keeps rendering the old art. So RigCatalog points at
# the registered copies and declares them as this kit's prerequisites, and materialising these
# locally to run the rig (see IMPORT.md) must never be committed.
isoSolid.js
fuelRig.js
